From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elena Maher <12779416+elenaOnline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:10:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpui: Add Window::paint_image_transformed

Images could only be drawn as axis-aligned quads: PolychromeSprite had no
transformation, unlike MonochromeSprite (used by paint_svg). A canvas
showing rotated, skewed or mirrored images had to resample them on the CPU
for every rotation and zoom.

PolychromeSprite gets the same `transformation` field, and
Window::paint_image_transformed passes one through (paint_image is the
identity case). For a transformed sprite the vertex shaders grow the quad
by one device pixel, and the fragment shaders evaluate the rounded-rect
SDF in the sprite's own space and divide it by its screen-space gradient,
so edges and corner radii (which may become ellipses) stay anti-aliased
under any rotation, scale or skew. Untransformed sprites keep their
geometry and SDF.

Sprite samples are clamped to the sprite's own atlas tile. Scaled images
used to blend their edge pixels with neighbouring atlas texels (a dark
fringe on straight-alpha tiles), and a transformed sprite's margin lies
entirely outside its tile.

The scene culls and orders transformed sprites by the bounding box of
their transformed bounds (Primitive::painted_bounds) instead of the
untransformed bounds, which may lie anywhere.

Window::with_element_opacity becomes public so callers can fade images and
emoji, which take no color.

Metal, WGSL (validated by the gpui_wgpu naga tests) and HLSL (unvalidated)
shaders are updated alike.
